# Setup — <PLUGIN_NAME>

This plugin needs the following **universal dependencies** (tools you install once on your
machine). The plugin does **not** install them for you: on start it detects what is missing,
asks your permission, and cannot be used until they are present.

## Required

| Dependency | What it does (plain terms) | Detect | Install |
|---|---|---|---|
| `<name>` | <what it does> | `<check-command>` | `<install-command>` |

## How the gate works

- On session start, `hooks/preflight-deps.py` checks each dependency.
- If any is missing, it tells Claude to **ask you for permission** to install it — naming the
  tool, its purpose, and the command. Nothing is installed without your explicit yes.
- If you decline, the plugin reports that it **cannot be used** until the dependency exists.

## Declared deps file

The checked list lives in `hooks/required-deps.json`:

```json
[
  {"name": "<name>", "check": "<executable-on-PATH>", "explain": "<plain purpose>", "install": "<command>"}
]
```
